   "text": "This SMILES was read region by region from the drawing. It describes a PROTAC-type molecule built from a VHL-type ligand, a linker, and an aminopyridazine\u2013phenol end.\n\n- **VHL end:** a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl group sits on a para-substituted benzylamide. The amide nitrogen is attached to a 4-hydroxyproline, with the hydroxyl wedged and the carboxamide bond hashed. I used the standard (2S,4R) form for these two centres.\n- **Acyl group:** the proline nitrogen is acylated by a CH carrying an isopropyl group and an isoxazol-5-yl ring. This carbon is drawn with plain bonds, so it has no stereo label.\n- **Linker:** the isoxazole carries an oxygen at C3 that connects to a cyclohexane. The cyclohexane is 1,4-disubstituted, with the oxygen hashed and the piperidine nitrogen wedged. That is the trans arrangement, which I wrote as `O[C@H]3CC[C@H](N...)CC3`. The piperidine is 4-substituted by a pyrimidin-5-yl ring.\n- **Bicycle:** the pyrimidine C2 is bonded to the bridging nitrogen (N8) of a 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane. The other nitrogen (N3) bonds to the pyridazine.\n- **Pyridazine end:** the pyridazine carries an amino group and a 2-hydroxyphenyl group.\n\nThe stereo marks on the proline and cyclohexane were set by comparison with remembered SMILES for similar fragments, not derived from the drawing's wedge geometry atom by atom.\n\nSMILES: Cc1ncsc1-c1ccc(CNC(=O)[C@@H]2C[C@@H](O)CN2C(=O)C(C(C)C)c2cc(O[C@H]3CC[C@H](N4CCC(CC4)c4cnc(nc4)N4C5CCC4CN(C5)c4cc(-c5ccccc5O)nnc4N)CC3)no2)cc1"
